DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       ppaammttooppddbbiimmgg reads a Netpbm image as input and produced a Palm Pilot Im‐
       age Viewer image (and Image record in a PDB file) as output.

       If the Netpbm image is black and white, the Pilot image is  monochrome.
       Otherwise, the Pilot image is either 4-level or 16-level grayscale, de‐
       pending on the --44ddeepptthh option.



OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In addition to the options common to all programs  based  on  libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common  Options  ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩  ), ppaammttooppddbbiimmgg recognizes
       the following command line options:




       --ttiittllee==_t_e_x_t
              The title of the image, to be included in the image.


       --ccoommpprreesssseedd

       --uunnccoommpprreesssseedd

       --mmaayybbeeccoommpprreesssseedd
              You may specify only one of these.  --ccoommpprreesssseedd says to generate
              the  image in compressed format.  --uunnccoommpprreesssseedd says to generate
              the image in uncompressed format.  --mmaayybbeeccoommpprreesssseedd says to gen‐
              erate  whichever  format  is  smaller (the compression algorithm
              sometimes actually makes the data larger).


       --44ddeepptthh
              This option makes  ppaammttooppddbbiimmgg  create  the  image  in  16-level
              grayscale (4 bits per pixel) format.  If you don't specify this,
              ppaammttooppddbbiimmgg uses 4-level (2 bits per pixel) format.

              This option has no effect when the  input  is  black  and  white
              (maxval  1).  In that case, ppaammttooppddbbiimmgg generates the monochrome
              (1 bit per pixel) format regardless.


       --nnootteeffiillee==_f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
              Attach the note in the specified file to the image.

              If you don't specify this, ppaammttooppddbbiimmgg does not attach any note.




